From 086d4f222eec9d0517e71c1177f5213db8d1b377 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 19:19:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Reaper v1.7.1: widen Network Map grey box (owner-directed
 follow-up)

The first pass widened the status panel within the fixed 740px .NM_table box; the
owner confirmed the box itself is the constraint - there is empty gutter to its
right and the client-status column still forced a horizontal scrollbar. Widen the
whole map box .NM_table 740px -> 800px so both 50% columns gain room (360->390px),
and widen the shared status panel 340->370px (content 330px >> 293px client card).
+60px matches the marked empty gutter, so no page-level h-scroll. CSS override only.
---
 .../src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css  | 26 ++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css b/release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css
index 0d6c06ae36..4fbffedfcf 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css
+++ b/release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css
@@ -800,16 +800,18 @@ body.bg,.container.no_highlights,.content_container{background:transparent!impor
    overflowing (reaper_content.css is loaded inside the statusframe document). */
 #client_list_Block{max-height:600px!important;overflow-y:auto!important;overflow-x:hidden!important}
 /* v1.7.1 (owner-reported): Network Map "Client status" panel showed a horizontal
-   scrollbar + badges spilling past the right edge. The stock panel shell is 320px
-   (#statusframe iframe + .NM_radius_bottom_container + .statusTitle, all width:320px,
-   margin-left:45px), but the global reaper body padding (16px 20px = 40px horiz,
-   reaper_content.css:23) shrinks the clients.asp content box to 280px while the stock
-   client card (.clientBg, device-map.css:565) is a FIXED 293px -> ~13px overflow, the
-   float:right connect/band badges landing at the spill edge. FIX = widen the panel
-   shell to 340px (content box 300px > 293px card, 7px slack) and reclaim the oversized
-   45px left margin to 15px so the wider panel still fits its 360px map column
-   (15+340=355 <= 360; stock 45+320=365 already overhung by 5px, so this is tighter,
-   not looser - no #NM_table (740px) overflow). !important beats the iframe inline width.
-   Panel is shared by all device-map views (router/internet/disk/...): all just gain room. */
-#statusframe,.NM_radius_bottom_container,.statusTitle{width:340px!important}
+   scrollbar + badges spilling past the right edge. Root cause: the stock client card
+   (.clientBg, device-map.css:565) is a FIXED 293px, but the panel column was too
+   narrow to hold it (stock 320px shell minus 40px reaper body padding = 280px content).
+   FIX (owner-directed): widen the whole grey Network-Map box (.NM_table, stock 740px)
+   into the empty space on its right, so BOTH 50%-columns gain room; then widen the
+   shared status panel shell to match. 800px box (padding 10 -> 780 inner) => 390px
+   columns => 370px panel (margin-left 15 + 370 = 385 <= 390 column; content box
+   370-40 = 330px >> 293px card, ample slack, no h-scrollbar). The 45px stock left
+   margin is cut to 15px so the wider panel stays inside its column. !important beats
+   the iframe inline width. The panel is shared by every device-map view
+   (router/internet/disk/System Status/...): all simply gain room. +60px over stock
+   matches the empty gutter in the owner's screenshot, so no page-level h-scroll. */
+.NM_table{width:800px!important}
+#statusframe,.NM_radius_bottom_container,.statusTitle{width:370px!important}
 .NM_radius_bottom_container,.statusTitle{margin-left:15px!important}
-- 
